WEBVTT

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:09.890
One more out! One more out!

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:19.880
<i>The clover,</i>

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:22.200
<i>a perennial of the legume family.</i>

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.020
<i>The four-leafed specimen is said to bring good luck.</i>

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:46.340
Fifth graders like you shouldn't be staring at that kind of stuff.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:49.340
Go deliver the balls over to the Tsukishimas already!

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:53.540
Boys mature by using their imaginations, you know.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.250
Just get going already!

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:24.170
I guess it finally broke.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.470
Hey, you. Do you guys sell hose nozzles?

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:31.270
Water spraying hasn't officially been approved as a sport yet, I'm afraid.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.400
And hey, don't "hey you" me!
I'm a year older than you!

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.290
Sure thing.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.520
That was close. I almost knocked it over.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.000
Aoba, Momiji,

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.600
come eat your snacks.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.190
Okay!

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:47.300
What happened, Ko?

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.670
You're drenched!

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:50.460
Well, I came to make a delivery...

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.090
Dad's waiting inside.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.240
Sure thing.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:55.670
Hey, Ko. Thanks for the hard work.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:58.110
We're getting our next shipment in two days,

00:03:58.110 --> 00:03:59.820
so these'll have to do for now, he said.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.520
All righty.

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.580
You want to play a little?

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.130
I guess I'll try here.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:24.100
Ko!

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:27.980
Take me to swim class on your bike, Ko!

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:37.360
Come on, what are you standing around for?

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:38.760
We have to hurry!

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:45.150
Come on, hurry! I'm going to be late!

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:47.370
What happened to <i>your</i> bike?

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:49.090
I got a flat tire yesterday.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:51.150
They're friendly, as usual.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.760
I don't get what she sees in him.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.500
It's fate.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.720
They were born on the same day, in the same hospital,

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.640
and were right next to each other from the moment they were born.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:02.370
Whoa!

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:05.960
Hold on tight, or you'll fall off!

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:07.890
Okay.

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:10.580
N-Not <i>that</i> tight, otherwise I can't steer!

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.720
Don't you two look nice together.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:17.110
Are you guys on a date?

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:18.250
As if!

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:21.320
I'm just taking her to swim class.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.530
That's perfect, then.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:25.900
Come join our team when you're done.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.990
We're a little short on people today.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:30.490
No way, man! Baseball's too much work.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:30.970
What?

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:32.880
You punk!

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:36.640
Weren't you the one who suggested that we make a team in class?

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:38.300
Oh yeah,

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:42.910
thanks for buying the gear and uniforms from our store.

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:46.450
Don't tell me you suggested it just so you could sell those to us?!

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:50.720
He gets a bigger allowance whenever he brings in a big order.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:51.360
Much obliged.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.490
How dare you trick us!

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:56.490
It may be tough being low on members, but good luck!

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:58.430
You punk! I oughta—

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:02.370
A date, huh? That sounds fun, too.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:06.120
Didn't I tell you not to hang on too tight?

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:08.120
If we keep running into people we know, we could—

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:10.240
Oh look, it's someone we know.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.950
Isn't that Akaishi from Class 4?

00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:24.110
Yeah, did you know?

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:26.000
Did I know what?

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.420
He's the strongest fighter in our grade.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:35.200
Did you also know that he has a crush on you?

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:41.000
I'll be done by five.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.260
Yeah, and?

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:44.180
Oh yeah.

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.450
That's for coming to pick me up.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:55.510
I-I didn't say I was coming to pick you up!

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:58.160
I'll be done by five, okay?

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:00.590
By five.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.560
<i>I'm not saying this just because she kissed me on the cheek,</i>

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:13.200
<i>but Tsukishima Wakaba is the cutest girl in my class.</i>

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:16.130
<i>No, probably in the entire grade.</i>

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:19.950
<i>So there are a lot of guys who like her,</i>

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:26.420
<i>like Akaishi, the strongest fighter in our grade...</i>

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:28.890
<i>Hayashi, the third-strongest fighter...</i>

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:31.360
<i>and Nawata, the fifth-strongest.</i>

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:34.030
Um...

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:41.540
Sorry I left you hanging, fellow Doors teammates.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:43.500
Why are <i>you</i> here?

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:48.030
I haven't once forgotten about this team, you know.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.570
This is to prove it.

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:53.510
I always wear the Doors uniform, so I can be a beacon of strength for you guys everywhere I go.

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:55.850
You're just wearing it as an everyday shirt, aren't you?

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:00.920
Listen, you guys.

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:03.450
The most important thing in baseball is teamwork.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.660
When one of the members is in trouble, everyone should help him out.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:12.600
Isn't that right, Mr. Second-Strongest
in Our Grade, Nakanishi?

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:18.100
It's the bottom of the fifth, with the score tied 5-5.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.660
It's the Doors' turn to attack.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:23.080
My my, isn't this a thrilling game?

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:26.610
This would have been a one-sided game if it wasn't for your four errors!

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.380
Well sor-ry.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:32.050
I've never played baseball or even played catch before.

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:33.970
You've never even played catch?

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:35.940
This inning will be our chance.

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:38.130
It's my turn to bat.

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:46.360
All right.

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:50.300
<i>I may have never played in games, or even played catch before,</i>

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:53.220
<i>but I've been swinging the bat since I was three</i>

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.210
<i>at Tsukishima Batting Center!</i>

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:00.460
Strike!

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:01.910
What kind of pitch was that?

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:04.100
That's what you call a good ol' fastball.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.120
It was right down the middle, too.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.320
They're gone now.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:10.760
It's the bottom of the sixth.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:14.580
The Doors are trailing by one, with no outs and a man on first.

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.410
Will they make a comeback?

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.700
If it weren't for your six errors—

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.200
And here's Nakanishi, their cleanup batter.

00:09:22.600 --> 00:09:25.000
It's going to center field!

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:27.710
Ball!

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:28.870
Ball!

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:30.950
Four balls!

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:34.030
We have no outs, and the bases are loaded!

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.950
Substitution!

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:41.010
Akaishi...

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.090
Watching you guys made me want to play,

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:45.620
so I asked these guys if I could join their team.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:53.490
That was amazing!

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:55.250
Of course.

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:59.140
He used to be the top pitcher at a famous Little League team up until a while ago.

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:00.430
Up until a while ago?

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:01.210
Yeah.

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:04.560
Until he punched out another pitcher and got kicked out.

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:08.210
Batting eighth, Kitamura.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:13.130
Akaishi asks,

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:15.730
"What's your relationship with Tsukishima Wakaba?"

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:18.200
W-We're just neighbors.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:19.280
Is that all?

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:20.290
Of course it is.

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:22.250
You better not be lying!

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:23.800
I wouldn't lie...

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:25.200
Hey, Ko!

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:29.200
I gave you a kiss, but you still didn't come to pick me up!

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:39.010
W-Well, this is actually...

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:43.700
What kind of pitch was that?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.720
That was easily over 100km/h!

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:48.920
Grade-schoolers aren't supposed to be able to pitch like that!

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:53.860
<i>I may have never played in games, or even played catch before,</i>

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:56.290
<i>but I've been swinging the bat since I was three.</i>

00:10:56.680 --> 00:11:01.600
<i>I've been hitting pitches upwards of 100 km/h at the Tsukishima Batting Center almost every day!</i>

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:13.350
All right!

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:13.340
A grand slam home run!

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:35.520
What do you want me to do?

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:36.990
We're playing catch.

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:38.000
Catch?

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:42.240
You've shown me that you can bat at the game yesterday,

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:45.410
but you won't be useful to us unless you can play defense as well!

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:48.430
Like I said, I've never played catch before.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:49.680
Then get used to it.

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:50.510
Why?

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:51.920
Shut up and play!

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:54.850
Hey, Aoba, can you get the ball for me?

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:57.720
Hey, Aoba!

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:18.980
I didn't know Aoba could throw so well.

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:22.990
I think she's even been playing with a bunch of fourth-grade guys lately.

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:24.800
She's pitching.

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:26.920
She's loved baseball ever since she was little.

00:12:27.530 --> 00:12:30.080
Your dad made it to Koshien as a high school player, right?

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.290
Pretty much.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:35.520
He said it was his dream to raise a son to become a professional baseball player.

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:38.360
But more importantly, let's exchange presents!

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:41.980
Can we stop doing this?

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:43.650
I never know what to get you.

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:44.840
No way!

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:48.040
This is an important event which happens only once a year!

00:12:52.340 --> 00:12:54.990
I can go change it for a different one if you don't like it.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:56.820
Nah, it's just barely okay.

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:57.920
Just barely, huh?

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:00.580
A clock <i>again</i>?

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:02.200
You got me one last year, too.

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:04.820
I didn't think having just one was enough for you, Ko.

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:06.130
Geez.

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:10.260
Happy June 10th Birthday!

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:17.150
She's so pretty.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.940
Really? Looks like a normal wedding dress to me.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:22.610
I'm sure those two are going to be happy.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:26.040
They got married on our birthday, after all.

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.400
It's a 3-2 count.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.250
Just one hit, and they could make a comeback here!

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:37.740
The summer's Koshien could be decided...

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:37.740
It's been a while since I've been in your room, Ko.

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:38.760
Really?

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:41.560
What happened to all the plastic models that used to be here?

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:44.200
They got all jumbled up together, so I stuck them in the closet.

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:47.110
You used to like airplanes, too, didn't you?

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:49.130
And trains before that.

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:50.800
Oh yeah,

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:55.010
you also wanted to be the manager of an aquarium because you used to like big fishes, right?

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:58.380
And a zookeeper before that.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:06.180
I wonder what you'll be when you grow up.

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:07.600
Who knows.

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:09.880
My hobbies change pretty often, you know.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:10.840
What about baseball?

00:14:10.840 --> 00:14:13.530
That's just me hanging out with the guys.

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:20.270
I can't wait to see what kind of an adult you'll become.

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:24.500
What are you sticking on my wall?

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:28.300
It's a list of presents I want each year, starting next year.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.690
A list?

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:31.940
This way you'll know what to get me.

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:37.280
Oh, can I borrow this cap when I go to camp?

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:40.070
Sure, but it's a little dirty.

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:41.980
That's fine.

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:44.490
How do I look?

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:54.440
<i>Tsukishima Wakaba is the cutest girl in my class.</i>

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:58.610
<i>No, probably the entire grade.</i>

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:07.720
<i>No, probably...</i>

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:14.390
I should get going.

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:16.700
Already?

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:17.780
Why don't you stay longer?

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:19.590
It's past nine, you know!

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:20.990
She's right.

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:23.220
Besides, you have to get up early tomorrow.

00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:25.140
I'll walk you home, then.

00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:26.930
It's okay, I live right down the street.

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:28.250
Yeah!

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:31.190
You should be more worried about getting back if you walk him home.

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:33.270
I'll walk you out to the road over there, then.

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:36.210
Fine, do what you want.

00:15:39.340 --> 00:15:42.190
I'll be back by the evening two days from now, okay?

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:43.590
Yeah. From camp, right?

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:46.540
We're going to go to the summer festival the day after that, okay?

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:47.620
Sure.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:50.550
Have fun at camp, then.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:51.990
Ko!

00:15:58.550 --> 00:15:59.620
Good night!

00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:05.950
Good night.

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:29.700
I'm surprised you haven't gone home yet today.

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:32.420
Oh I get it.

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:34.470
It's because Wakaba's gone, isn't it?

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.710
As if!

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:48.280
Both the batting center and the café were closed?

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:49.300
Yeah.

00:16:49.300 --> 00:16:52.020
Their regular day off was supposed to be yesterday.

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:53.280
That's strange.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:56.720
I could have sworn they were open when I passed by this afternoon.

00:16:57.340 --> 00:17:00.460
That reminds me, Wakaba's coming back tomorrow, right?

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:02.790
Yeah, she said tomorrow evening.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:03.760
I see.

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:06.190
But it really is hot today, isn't it?

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:08.760
I got the bath ready for you, so go wash off some sweat, okay?

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:09.670
'Kay.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:16.470
They must be rehearsing for the summer festival.

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:28.950
<i>Good night!</i>

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:55.450
They play so hard each day even under the scorching weather, huh.

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:57.690
<i>And now, time for a news update:</i>

00:17:57.690 --> 00:18:00.110
<i>Amidst the increase in water-related accidents around the nation,</i>

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:04.360
<i>a girl has drowned while attending swim camp in the Minagawa Valley,</i>

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:07.970
<i>and was pronounced dead after being carried to a hospital late last night.</i>

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:12.620
<i>The victim was a fifth-grader from Tokyo's Senkawa-kita Elementary School,</i>

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:14.780
<i>Tsukishima Wakaba, age eleven.</i>

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:17.400
<i>It's been reported that Wakaba got caught up in a current</i>

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:21.690
<i>and drowned while trying to help a younger girl whose legs were caught in the deep end.</i>

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:25.250
<i>Now back to our Koshien coverage.</i>

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:26.310
<i>It is now the 7th day—</i>

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:14.930
Where are you going, Ko?

00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:17.680
To the summer festival.

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:19.630
The summer festival? You can't be—

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:22.570
Do you have money?

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:24.030
Um, no.

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:27.450
Don't waste it, okay?

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:28.480
I won't.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:50.060
<i>I'll be back by the evening two days from now, okay?</i>

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:57.700
<i>We're going to go to the summer festival the day after that, okay?</i>

00:19:59.070 --> 00:20:00.830
Hey, little man,

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:03.250
you shouldn't be walking around with your head down like that.

00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:04.340
Hey, Mister?

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:05.650
Yeah?

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:08.260
What should I do now?

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:08.980
Huh?

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:41.480
<i>Akaishi...</i>

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:54.490
<i>I get it now.</i>

00:20:55.260 --> 00:20:57.260
<i>It's not hard at all.</i>

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:01.000
<i>I just have to cry.</i>

00:23:02.970 --> 00:23:04.180
<i>The clover,</i>

00:23:04.180 --> 00:23:06.120
<i>a perennial of the legume family.</i>

00:23:06.120 --> 00:23:09.340
<i>The four-leafed specimen is said to bring good luck.</i>

00:23:11.470 --> 00:23:13.330
<i>We're playing Aoba's team?</i>

00:23:13.330 --> 00:23:15.640
<i>Yeah, and you're pitching, Ko.</i>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:18.780
<i>You having fun pitching like that?</i>

00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:21.620
<i>I don't find baseball the least bit fun.</i>

00:23:21.620 --> 00:23:24.070
<i>Why can't you be friends with Ko?</i>

00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:26.430
<i>Wakaba liked him best, you know.</i>

00:23:26.430 --> 00:23:27.680
<i>That's exactly why.</i>

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:31.240
<i>You shouldn't treat Ko like those other guys!</i>

00:23:31.240 --> 00:23:33.080
<i>Once he gets serious...</i>

00:23:34.030 --> 00:23:36.170
<i>Next time, on Cross Game Episode Two:</i>

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:38.360
<i>I Hate Him!</i>
